.TH TAILTRAY 1 "November 2025" "TailTray 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tailtray \- Tailscale GUI for KDE Plasma
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tailtray
.RI [ OPTION... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TailTray
is a system tray GUI application for Tailscale on Linux, providing the same features as the Windows Tailscale client. It is designed specifically for KDE Plasma desktop environment running on Wayland.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help options
.TP
.BR \-\-help\-gtk
Show GTK+ options
.TP
.BR \-\-display=DISPLAY
X display to use
.SH FEATURES
.IP \(bu 2
Device Management: View and search all devices in your Tailscale network
.IP \(bu 2
Exit Node Selection: Enable/disable exit nodes with a full selection dialog
.IP \(bu 2
Taildrop: Send files to devices on your network
.IP \(bu 2
Tailscale SSH: SSH connections with terminal integration
.IP \(bu 2
Troubleshooting: Diagnostics, connectivity tests, and log viewing
.IP \(bu 2
MagicDNS: DNS name display and automatic resolution
.IP \(bu 2
System Tray: KDE Plasma system tray with right-click menu
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files are stored in
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tailtray/
(default: ~/.config/tailtray/)
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/tailtray/config.json
User configuration file
.TP
.B ~/.cache/tailtray/tailtray.log
Application log file
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for user configuration files
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X display to use (for X11 compatibility)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tailscale (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
TailTray Contributors
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at <https://github.com/yourusername/tailtray/issues>